**Medium Severity**

<!-- DESCRIPTION START -->
`hasDatabaseURLSecret` uses `u.Query().Get("password")` which is case-sensitive, while the `databaseURLPattern` regex that feeds it is case-insensitive (`(?i)`). A database URL like `REDACTED` would be matched by the pattern but `Get("password")` returns empty for the key `Password`. The three sibling detectors (`hasJDBCPassword`, `hasKeywordDSNPassword`, `hasSemicolonConnectionPassword`) all delegate to `hasNonPlaceholderPasswordAssignment` which uses the case-insensitive `passwordAssignmentRegex`, so they handle `Password`, `PASSWORD`, and `pwd` variants correctly. This inconsistency creates a credential-leak gap specific to non-JDBC database URLs with a non-lowercase `password` query parameter name.
<!-- DESCRIPTION END -->

<!-- BUGBOT_BUG_ID: 8da3b6d0-a861-4d3e-bcd1-4d0151a9a163 -->

